WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.730
- My name is Sten Vermund.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.340
I serve as Dean of the Yale
School of Public Health.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.780
But I wanted to just highlight

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.340
the partnership of Yale University

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.723
with the American University of Beirut.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.117
The AUB dates back more than 150 years.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.975
Founded.

00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:25.808
In 1866.

00:00:27.906 --> 00:00:29.073
And there were

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.100
American's who were literally fundraising

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.820
to start this school in Beirut

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.570
during the American Civil
War just to give you a sense.

00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:42.665
And just after the American Civil War.

00:00:42.665 --> 00:00:43.498
So.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:48.170
The university has been

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:52.140
a highly stable academic force

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.550
with American accreditation.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:01:00.253
It was originally accredited
by New York State Educational.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.220
Entities.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.400
And all the many years

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.000
with all the trials and
tribulations of the Middle East

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:16.220
AUB has maintained its
leadership role in academia.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.150
And we're proud that
that includes medicine

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.463
and it includes public health and nursing.

00:01:23.463 --> 00:01:27.800
So let me turn it over
to Doctor Khoshnood.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:32.800
We have been proud to be
working with AUB for many years.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.820
And we'll be hearing from its
former dean in just a moment.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.480
Doctor Khoshnood.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.550
- Thank you so much Stan.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.800
Again I'm Kaveh Khoshnood

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:48.340
Associate Professor Yale
School of Public Health.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.570
I've had the pleasure
of knowing doctor Iman

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.670
for over a decade.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:56.260
And I'm delighted to introduce him to you.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.670
Doctor Iman Nuwayhid is
Professor of Public Health

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.470
and Occupation at Environmental Health

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.520
at the Faculty of Health Sciences

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.820
at the American University of Beirut.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.170
He served as the dean for 12 years

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:15.910
at the faculty health
sciences from 2008 to 2020.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.510
He's co-editor of the landmark book

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.080
on "Public Health in the Arab World",

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.560
Cambridge University press 2012.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.560
Add he's a co-chair of the
Lancet-AUB Commission on Syria.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.640
His research focuses on
the health of workers

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.000
including working children,
environment and health,

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.363
and conflict and health.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.090
I'm so delighted that doctor Iman

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.600
who's on sabbatical right
now decided to come to Yale,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.220
he's currently in New Haven

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.830
and is teaching the first ever course

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:54.763
called Public Health in the
Arab World at Yale College.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.090
Doctor Iman thank you
so much for joining us,

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.340
I'll turn it over to you.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.330
