perhaps political system ever.

00:59:01.900 --> 00:59:04.330
It's sectarian, what can you do?

00:59:04.330 --> 00:59:09.120
I think what we can do is continue to work

00:59:09.120 --> 00:59:13.080
in spite of these obstacles.

00:59:13.080 --> 00:59:14.650
Continue dreaming of a better

00:59:17.850 --> 00:59:20.140
society and of a better country.

00:59:20.140 --> 00:59:25.070
For you as a physician
look beyond the clinical,

00:59:25.070 --> 00:59:29.460
look beyond the disease to
try to look at this wider

00:59:30.470 --> 00:59:32.250
disease that we're all

00:59:33.260 --> 00:59:35.750
suffering from which is social injustice.

00:59:35.750 --> 00:59:36.810
I think these are the concepts

00:59:36.810 --> 00:59:39.140
that we need to start introducing.

00:59:39.140 --> 00:59:41.808
We haven't done enough and
that's why you're right,

00:59:41.808 --> 00:59:44.320
maybe we're not ready.

00:59:44.320 --> 00:59:46.090
We don't know how to deal with it.

00:59:46.090 --> 00:59:47.900
But I think we need to challenge ourselves

00:59:47.900 --> 00:59:50.510
and commit to that to start
looking there different.

00:59:50.510 --> 00:59:53.780
And this is not about Lebanon.

00:59:53.780 --> 00:59:56.440
I think it's the U.S. as much as Europe

00:59:56.440 --> 01:00:00.180
as much as Africa, as
much as the Middle East,

01:00:00.180 --> 01:00:01.990
as much as Asia.

01:00:01.990 --> 01:00:04.830
We all need to do that.

01:00:04.830 --> 01:00:07.350
I see a note here from a different

01:00:07.350 --> 01:00:09.830
saying we need to address the
politics of public health.

01:00:09.830 --> 01:00:10.880
True.

01:00:10.880 --> 01:00:12.740
We need to not to be shy

01:00:13.678 --> 01:00:17.610
to shy away from talking politics.

01:00:17.610 --> 01:00:21.460
Not engaging in the politics necessarily

01:00:21.460 --> 01:00:23.690
but talking politics and making sure

01:00:23.690 --> 01:00:26.620
that there is a political
context and dimension

01:00:26.620 --> 01:00:27.500
to public health.

01:00:27.500 --> 01:00:30.010
It's not a technical field.

01:00:30.010 --> 01:00:33.490
Politic, health is not a technical issue.

01:00:33.490 --> 01:00:37.270
Health is a political
issue, is a social issue,

01:00:37.270 --> 01:00:40.550
and it's determined by
the conditions we live in,

01:00:40.550 --> 01:00:44.440
we work in, by all these
different structures

01:00:44.440 --> 01:00:47.970
that determine our lives and our futures

01:00:47.970 --> 01:00:49.563
and the future of our children.

01:00:50.620 --> 01:00:52.233
- Last question from Feha.

01:00:56.051 --> 01:00:58.840
- Thank you so much for the presentation.

01:00:58.840 --> 01:01:00.170
My name is Feha from Sudan.

01:01:00.170 --> 01:01:03.390
It's actually a comment
more than a question.

01:01:03.390 --> 01:01:05.810
I just wanted to say at this point,

01:01:05.810 --> 01:01:07.120
first thank you for presenting this

01:01:07.120 --> 01:01:08.849
because I didn't know
the situation in Lebanon

01:01:08.849 --> 01:01:10.480
and it's so much replicated

01:01:10.480 --> 01:01:13.100
at many of in the
countries in the regions.

01:01:13.100 --> 01:01:15.530
One of the thing that we are
start talking about in Sudan

01:01:15.530 --> 01:01:18.250
that now we need to work
outside the health field

01:01:18.250 --> 01:01:19.550
to tackle the issues of health.

01:01:19.550 --> 01:01:22.660
So we start talk about now
we need to politicize health,

01:01:22.660 --> 01:01:24.150
to make sure the politician nowaday

01:01:24.150 --> 01:01:26.490
consider health as part of their agenda

01:01:26.490 --> 01:01:28.440
which is not really happening.

01:01:28.440 --> 01:01:32.060
Because when the
political decision happens

01:01:32.060 --> 01:01:34.166
and the health have been impacted

01:01:34.166 --> 01:01:37.300
there is no actual action happen

01:01:37.300 --> 01:01:40.370
in term of what can we do and so on.

01:01:40.370 --> 01:01:42.420
So thank you very much
for this presentation

01:01:42.420 --> 01:01:43.535
and we are looking forward

01:01:43.535 --> 01:01:46.970
for more discussion in this actual.

01:01:46.970 --> 01:01:49.020
- And I look forward to hearing you

01:01:49.020 --> 01:01:50.390
talking about Sudan again

01:01:50.390 --> 01:01:53.620
in the context of Africa
and the Arab world.

01:01:53.620 --> 01:01:58.270
'Cause your situation is as
complex if not more than ours.

01:01:58.270 --> 01:01:59.120
Good luck to you.

01:02:00.900 --> 01:02:02.770
- Thank you for all the participant,

01:02:02.770 --> 01:02:04.200
thank you so much doctor Iman.

01:02:04.200 --> 01:02:06.670
We should've made this
much longer (Kaveh laughs)

01:02:06.670 --> 01:02:10.110
than an hour because there's
lots of lots of interest

01:02:10.110 --> 01:02:11.610
in conversation with you.

01:02:11.610 --> 01:02:14.770
But hopefully we will have
another talk with doctor Iman.

01:02:14.770 --> 01:02:17.140
Thank you so much, really appreciate it.

01:02:17.140 --> 01:02:18.326
- Thank you all.

01:02:18.326 --> 01:02:19.659
Appreciate that.

